#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:45
msgid ""
"image:kislev/logo.webp[width=100,height=113,float=\"right\"] The land of "
"Kislev lies in the north-eastern portion of the Old World between towering "
"mountains to the east, the barren wastes of the Troll Country to the west "
"and the borders of the Empire to the south. Dense pine forests give way to "
"scattered birch forests and desolate tundra to the north. It is an old "
"saying that in Kislev the winters are long, the snow lies deep, and enemies "
"are never far away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:56
msgid ""
"Kislev shares its southern border with the Empire but in every other "
"direction it is surrounded by deadly foes. The eastern mountains are full of "
"goblins and other greenskins whilst beyond the lands are home to savage "
"marauder tribes.  To the north-west is the land of Norsca – barbarians in "
"thrall to the Dark Gods. When the armies of Chaos gather Kislev lies "
"directly in their path between the forces of darkness and the lands to the "
"south. With typically grim humour Kislevites describe their land as lying "
"between the hammer and the anvil (meaning Chaos and the Empire)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:70
msgid ""
"Kislev is reckoned a backward and barbarous country by the people of the "
"southlands. Some even go as far as to say that the Kislevites are little "
"better than the savage marauder tribes themselves. There is some truth in "
"this – because the people of Kislev are an admixture of native Old Worlders "
"like the people of the Empire and a marauding Kurgan tribe called the "
"Gospodars. As with the tribes of Chaos there are those amongst the "
"Kislevites who possess the gift of prophecy and other sorcerous abilities. "
"The ruling family of the Tzars is descended directly from the Sorceress Khan-"
"Queens of the Gospodars.  Female members of the family often possess great "
"powers. This mixture of southern and northern blood makes the Kislevites "
"seem exotic and dangerous to the people of the Empire."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:81
msgid ""
"Many of the Tzar’s subjects are fierce nomadic horsemen and hunters rather "
"than settled farmers and town-dwelling traders.  These nomads are the most "
"savage of the Kislevites retaining both the ancient traditions and pure "
"blood of the Gospodars of old. The townships of Kislev are built mainly of "
"huge timbers.  Good building stone is rare whilst tall pine trees are "
"plentiful.  Only the largest cities have stone walls and imposing civic "
"buildings constructed from masonry. Gilded domes distinguish the temples of "
"the strange Kislevite gods from those of the Empire."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:90
msgid ""
"For many years the Tzars of Kislev have enjoyed the friendship of the "
"Emperor and the goodwill of the Dwarfs. The present ruler is the Tzarina "
"Katarina – a great sorceress known throughout the Old World as the Ice Queen "
"of Kislev. In her the old powers of the Khan-Queens have resurfaced and she "
"is both abhorred and feared by her people, especially by the nomadic tribes "
"who believe her to be favoured by the ancient gods of the Gospodars."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "Kislev army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$kislev.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[winged-lancers,†1]]1. Winged Lancers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:108
msgid ""
"Winged Lancers receive +1 Attack in the first round of every combat when "
"fighting to the front and are Immune to Terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[horse-archers-cossacks,†2]]2. Horse Archers, Cossacks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:112
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[bowmen,†3]]3. Bowmen"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:115
msgid ""
"One unit of Bowmen per full 1000 points can replace a unit of Axemen while "
"still counting for Axemen min/max value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[red-guard,†4]]4. Red Guard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:121
msgid ""
"In addition to traditional Kislevite long axes Red Guard are armed with "
"handguns. Count enemy armour values as one worse than normal when shot by a "
"handgun. So an armour value of 3+ counts as 4+, 4+ as 5+, and 5+ as 6+, "
"whilst an armour value of 6+ can’t save against a handgun."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[bears,†5]]5. Bears"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:126
msgid ""
"Bears are defined as infantry for rules purposes as this gives them the "
"appropriate mobility for such creatures, but they add +1 Attack when they "
"charge an enemy in the open in the same way as monsters and chariots."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:131
msgid ""
"A Bear unit can only give support and be supported by other Bear units and "
"must pursue retreating enemy where possible and must advance if they are "
"able to do so. Also, Bears never count as defended outside a dense terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:135
msgid ""
"Note that these rules apply only to Bear units – not to characters riding a "
"Bear or Shamans that have transformed in Monster Bear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[war-wagon,†6]]6. War Wagon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:142
msgid ""
"image:kislev/wagon-laagered.webp[width=250,height=253,float=\"right\"]"
"{empty} War Wagon. The War Wagon consists of a wagon stand and a horse team "
"stand. The unit must always be in one of two formations: a column with the "
"horse team in front of the wagon, or a laager with the horse team placed "
"beside the wagon edge to edge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:149
msgid ""
"The War Wagon cannot charge and moves 20cm at full pace. A War Wagon unit "
"moving more than 5cm must end its move in a column formation. After a "
"successful order, if at least one stand moves no more than 5cm, the unit may "
"end its move in laager formation. The War Wagon may enter laager formation "
"as part of an evade, following the 5cm movement restriction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:155
msgid ""
"Uniquely, the War Wagon attacks are shared between the stands: a total of 4 "
"melee attacks that can be directed from either the horse team or wagon stand "
"and a total of 4 shooting attacks with 360° vison. Count enemy armour values "
"as one worse than normal when shot by a War Wagon."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:160
msgid ""
"A War Wagon in column formation cannot pursue. Unlike other artillery it can "
"retreat from combat and is not destroyed if forced to do so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:167
msgid ""
"A War Wagon in laager formation counts as a defended unit, with no sides or "
"rear.  It cannot make way. It cannot be driven back or routed by shooting, "
"but roll for (defended) drive backs to see if it becomes confused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:174
msgid ""
"image:kislev/wagon-column.webp[width=132,height=499,float=\"right\"] A War "
"Wagon in laager formation will neither pursue nor retreat. If obliged to "
"retreat, it instead remains in place, is not destroyed, continues to count "
"as defended, and enemy stands do not receive any pursuit bonuses against it "
"in subsequent rounds of combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:180
msgid ""
"Either stand can be removed as causality. If the horse team stand is "
"removed, the wagon stand will count as in laager formation for the remainder "
"of the game. If the wagon stand is removed, the remaining horse team stand "
"has no armour, no attacks, and counts as in column formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:185
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:190
msgid ""
"Any Kislev infantry unit with a side edge of one stand touching wholly the "
"short edge of a laagered wagon stand counts as defended for shooting and "
"combat. This advantage applies only in the first round of combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:191
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[bear-mount,†7]]7. Bear Mount"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:193
msgid ""
"Generals, Heroes and Shamans can ride a Bear mount. The Bear adds +1 Attack "
"to that of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:194
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[yozhin,†8]]8. Yozhin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:200
msgid ""
"This creature has lived in swamps near Praag since the great incursion of "
"Chaos. Yozhin strongly hates any kind of Chaos, being (possibly) a Chaos-"
"twisted creature itself. Only powerful Shamans may summon Yozhin and make it "
"fight on their side. A single Shaman in the army can be assisted by Yozhin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:202
msgid "[.edit]#Yozhin may enter water, bogs or swamps without restriction.#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:205
msgid ""
"A unit that has been joined by [.edit]#a Shaman riding Yozhin# causes terror "
"in its enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:208
msgid "Yozhin adds +1 Attack to Shaman’s attacks value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:209
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[tzarina,†9]]9. Tzarina"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:212
msgid ""
"The General may be a Tzarina of the royal blood – perhaps Tzarina Katrina "
"herself. The Tzarina rides a horse-drawn sled – note this is not a chariot!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:216
msgid ""
"The Tzarina can cast spells like a Wizard and can carry a magic item "
"restricted to a Wizard if desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:221
msgid ""
"Once during the battle the Tzarina can add +1 to the dice when attempting to "
"cast a spell. The player must announce that the Tzarina’s special spell "
"casting bonus is being used before rolling for the spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:226
#, no-wrap
msgid "Kislev spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:229
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monster Bear!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:235
msgid ""
"_The Wizard transforms himself into a gigantic ferocious supernatural bear "
"and hurls himself into the enemy’s ranks._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:239
msgid ""
"The Wizard can cast this spell on himself if he has joined a unit that is "
"engaged in combat. The spell lasts for the duration of the following Combat "
"phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:244
msgid ""
"The unit causes terror and the Wizard gains a further +2 Attack bonus that "
"he adds to the unit in the regular way. Note that if the Tzarina uses this "
"spell she adds +4 Attacks: +2 as General and +2 from Monster Bear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:246
#, no-wrap
msgid "Icy Blast"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:252
msgid ""
"_An icy blast shoots from the Wizard’s outstretched arm and strikes his foes."
"_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:259
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on an enemy unit. The Wizard must be able to see his "
"target to use this spell. The spell cannot be directed at a unit engaged in "
"combat. The Icy Blast is treated like three ordinary shooting attacks except "
"that armour has no effect (all targets count as having no armour). A unit "
"can be driven back by an Icy Blast as with ordinary shooting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:261
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chill"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:267
msgid ""
"_A fierce chill envelops the unit, freezing its warriors and hindering its "
"ability to fight._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:274
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:254
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast upon an enemy unit that is engaged in combat and "
"which is within range. The Wizard does not have to be able to see the target "
"to cast the spell. The spell lasts for the duration of the following Combat "
"phase. Every stand in the unit, including characters that have joined the "
"unit, deducts −1 from its Attacks value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:276
#, no-wrap
msgid "Freeze"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:279
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:280
msgid "[.cost]#6+ to cast# [.points]#Range 60cm#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:282
msgid ""
"_An ill wind turns the enemy so brittle that wood, flesh and even iron "
"shatters and falls to the ground in splinters._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:286
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast at an enemy unit within range regardless of whether "
"the Wizard can see it or not. The spell cannot be directed at a unit engaged "
"in combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:291
msgid ""
"Roll a D6. If the score exceeds the number of hits that the target troop "
"type has then one stand is destroyed. If not then the target is unscathed. "
"If a stand is destroyed it is removed as a casualty.  A unit cannot be "
"driven back by Freeze."
msgstr ""
